    <statement><p>Find the sum of the series</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle 5 + \frac{5}{2} + \frac{5}{4} + ... + \frac{5}{2^{n-1}} + ...</m>.</p>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>10</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>a + ar + ar^2 + ... + ar^{n-1} + ...</m> 



with <m>a = 5</m> and <m>\displaystyle r=\frac{1}{2}</m>. 



The sum of the series is 
<m>\displaystyle \frac{5}{1-\frac{1}{2}} = \frac{10}{2-1} = 10</m>. 


</solution>
